{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DuCsoH7jt5o7HZ2fTMyH1J","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# warmups — technique log (days 1-30; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8): nothing below is a guarantee for TT/Mastery -- derive structure per field.\n5\t- Each day: one `blob.txt`; decode until the sentence `Nice work decoding this warmup! To solve, submit this exact answer\n6\t  to the Game Master: <slug>` appears. Slug `word-word-word-NN`, `kind=pattern`, `normalization=trim`, question `message`.\n7\t- The codec changes daily; the title/prompt is a pun naming it: D1 \"64\" base64; D2 \"half a turn\" ROT13; D3 \"sixteen\n8\t  fingers\" hex; D4 \"two sides\" binary; D5 decimal; D6 \"eight fingers\" octal; D7 \"Percent\"/\"address bar\" URL `%xx`; D8\n9\t  \"Entity\" `&#N;`; D9 \"Escape Room\" `\"\\uXXXX\"`; D10 \"Thirty-Two\" base32; D11 \"URL-friendly\" unpadded base64url; D12\n10\t  \"wrong end\" REVERSED; D13 \"A met Z\" Atbash; D14 \"Caesar took a week off\" +7; D15 \"Forty-Seven\" ROT47; D16 \"Sixteen\n11\t  ... Dot dot dot\" MORSE over HEX; D17 \"Five little a's and b's\" BACON 5-groups = hex nibbles; D18 \"Three rails\" RAIL\n12\t  FENCE 3/0; D19 \"Two bytes ... little one first\" hex of UTF-16LE `fffe`; D20 \"Same bar ... big one\" UTF-16BE `feff`;\n13\t  D21 \"A familiar wrapper. Something compressed\" GZIP in base64; D22 \"Another ... inflation\" ZLIB in base64; D23\n14\t  \"alphabet got bigger. Adobe\" ASCII85 `<~~>`; D24 \"The comma knows where to stop\" NETSTRINGS `1:N,`; D25 \"Every\n15\t  character has a point\" `U+004E`; D26 \"A very small language\" BRAINFUCK program (`+ - .`, one cell); D27 \"Ook. Ook?\n16\t  Ook!\" the same program in Ook! pairs; D28 \"Our sixteen-fingered friend is walking backwards.\" REVERSED HEX (char-wise);\n17\t  D29 \"Sixty-four invited thirteen over. Things got scrambled.\"/\"Rotten Base\" ROT13 OF BASE64; D30 \"That address bar\n18\t  problem? It happened twice.\"/\"Percent Percent\" URL `%xx` APPLIED TWICE (`%25%34%65` -> `%4e` -> `N`).\n19\t- Shape of the run: D1-D15, D23-D27 one layer; D16-D17, D19-D22, D28-D30 two, the pun naming BOTH (every number/word\n20\t  may be a layer or a key; \"familiar\"/\"invited over\" = a seen codec as the other layer; \"twice\" = the SAME codec\n21\t  again). Knob days (D20, D22, D27) turn one parameter of the day before. Families: base-N/char codes/escapes (D1-D11),\n22\t  free-text letter maps (D12-D15), carriers over hex (D16-D17), transposition (D18), byte representation (D19-D20),\n23\t  compression (D21-D22), bigger alphabet (D23), framing (D24), notation (D25), ESOLANGS (D26-D27, execute don't\n24\t  decode), then REMIXES D28-D30: 2-layer stacks of D1-D12 codecs (hex+rev, b64+rot13, url+url) cued by re-quoting an\n25\t  old riddle. On an unknown shape read the STRUCTURE (repeating unit, token shape, tiny operator alphabet) + the pun.\n26\t- Mastery is cumulative: day N = 5N-2 sets x N lines `NN<TAB>fragment`, line k = day k's codec over a mid-word fragment\n27\t  (line 26 = 166-217 B BF; 27 = 1672-2172 B Ook; 28 = 8-10 rev-hex chars; 29 = 8-char rot13'd b64 `nJkfoj==`; 30 =\n28\t  36-char double `%25%37%37...`; 148 x 30). Last line has no trailing newline; fragments join verbatim.\n29\t- Clocks: D1-D15 TT/Mastery ~5-9 s windows; since D16 mostly `deadline: null`, but the HARNESS kills solve.py at 60 s\n30\t  (D17, D21, D26, D30: live workers hand-decoded). D23/D25 Mastery first submit all-NN wrong (pre-decoded line). D28-D29\n31\t  TT/Mastery first try in < 10 s. D30 TT 3.0 s; Mastery 148 x 30 solve 65.9 s -> KILLED (line 30 pre-peeled, no\n32\t  DAYS[29]/[30]); a live worker's flat positional table (line k -> day k's decoder) got 148/148 on its first submit.\n33\t\n34\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n35\t- **Encoding per 