6-D17)** -- a charset-collapsing carrier over HEX of the UTF-8 text: D16 Morse\n70\t  (one space between symbols, symbols only `0-9A-F`), D17 Bacon lowercase `a`/`b` 5-groups `aaaaa`..`abbbb` (values\n71\t  0-15 = nibbles). Parse rule: carrier output that is hex / exactly 16 symbols / `a`-`p` -> nibbles -> `fromhex`;\n72\t  digits -> char codes; accept printable + slug. Any two-symbol group carrier: `warmups_codecs.twosym_dec`.\n73\t- **Order / transposition (D18)** -- same multiset, new order: single/TT whole sentence rail fence 3 rails offset 0;\n74\t  Mastery line 18 = the 6-8 char fragment rail-fenced ON ITS OWN (`p-pr5e6` -> `pper-56`). Parse rule: `rail_dec(t,3,0)`\n75\t  first, then r 2..11 x offsets, accept only a crib/slug hit; Mastery via `rail_free` in the slug-gated joint search.\n76\t  Any keyless permutation (columnar, route, skip) = enumerate keys, gate on crib/slug.\n77\t- **Text encoding / byte order under hex (D19-D20)** -- D19 single/TT one lowercase hex string `fffe` + UTF-16LE\n78\t  (`4e00 6900`), D20 `feff` + UTF-16BE (`004e 0069`). Mastery lines 19/20 each carry their OWN BOM (`fffe2d006a00...`,\n79\t  `feff00700065...`), both orders in one blob -> order from each line's BOM, never from the day. Parse rule (D19\n80\t  `_hex_utf16`, carried D20 unchanged): `fromhex`; check `fffe0000`/`0000feff` (UTF-32) and `efbbbf` first, then BOM\n81\t  `fffe`/`feff` -> `decode('utf-16')`; no BOM but NUL at every odd/even byte -> `utf-16-le`/`-be`; accept printable only.\n82\t  A latin-1 hex fallback gives `ÿþN\\x00i\\x00...` (no slug). No-BOM / UTF-32 / UTF-8-BOM / other outer layer: prebuilt.\n83\t- **Compressor under a text wrapper (D21-D22)** -- ONE std padded base64 string of a GZIP member (D21, `H4sIAAAAAAACA`)\n84\t  / a ZLIB `78da` stream (D22, `eNo`/`eNp`/`eNr`: match `eN`); Mastery lines 21/22 = 36-/20-char fragments, each its\n85\t  OWN member/stream. Parse rule (D21 `_b64z`, carried D22 unchanged): `[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]+={0,2}`, len%4 != 1 -> re-pad,\n86\t  urlsafe-decode -> sniff magic (`1f8b`, RFC 1950 `(b0<<8|b1)%31==0`, `BZh`, `fd377a585a`; else raw `wbits=-15`) ->\n87\t  decompress -> re-run the full decoder; whole blob BEFORE the numbered-line check + `register_free(\"b64z\", 21, ...)`.\n88\t- **Base-N alphabet size / armor (D23)** -- single/TT = ONE Adobe Ascii85 `<~...~>`, no newline/wraps/`z`, 141-143 B;\n89\t  Mastery line 23 = an 11-char `<~XXXXXXX~>` per fragment, EACH with its own delimiters. The `!`..`u` alphabet overlaps\n90\t  every printable codec, so the delimiters are the cue (bare a85 collides with ROT47 -> slug-gate). Parse rule (`_a85`):\n91\t  `<~..~>` -> `a85decode(t, adobe=True)`, else `a85decode` (z), `b85decode`, Z85 (translate to b85's alphabet); sniff\n92\t  magic, UTF-8 + slug gate; Mastery via `register_free(\"a85\", 23, fn)` on the RAW line (Pitfalls, D23).\n93\t- **Framing / length prefix (D24)** -- single/TT = ONE line of netstrings `<len>:<data>,`, no separators/newline, EVERY\n94\t  len = `1` (444 B, 4 B/char); the payload's own `,` `:` and spaces are data (`1:,,`, `1::,`, `1: ,`). Mastery line 24\n95\t  = the same over the fragment (`1:o,1:n,1:-,`), 810/810 prefixes `1`. Parse rule (`_netstr`): cursor loop -- `\\s*(\\d+):`\n96\t  at i, take EXACTLY `len` chars, require `,` (or end), advance; WHOLE text must parse (else None); never `split(',')`.\n97\t  Covers len > 1/mixed; tnetstrings/bencode/RESP/chunked/varint/indexed/RLE frames are prebuilt siblings.\n98\t- **Esoteric program + its SPELLING (D26-D27)** -- the blob is a PROGRAM; its output is the text. Program unchanged:\n99\t  ONE cell from 0, each char = a run of ONLY `+` or ONLY `-` = delta from the previous char, then `.`; no loops/`<>`/`,`.\n100\t  Spelling changed: D26 raw BF `+ - .` (~31 B/char; Mastery line 26 = 166-217 B); D27 Ook! `Ook.`/`Ook!` single-spaced,\n101\t  PAIRED from token 0, only `..` + / `!!` - / `!.` output, NO `Ook?` (~314 B/char; line 27 = 1672-2172 B, cell 0 again).\n102\t  Parse rule: tokenize 