o seen day codecs composed in either order (rot13 of base64, Atbash/rail of hex, base64 of ROT47, URL-encoded base64, Morse of base32, hex of reversed text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\"\n343:  {\"id\": \"mixed-segment-recap-blob\", \"concept\": \"finale recap: one single-solve blob made of segments in different seen codecs (unnumbered lines, separators, or a codec per segment)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Last days (D29-D31) may \n348:  {\"id\": \"program-output-redecode\", \"concept\": \"esolang output that is itself encoded (BF/Ook printing base64/hex/rot13/Morse/decimal codes) and programs under a seen wrapper (base64/hex/gzip of BF or Ook)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"\n352:  {\"id\": \"unseparated-token-bf\", \"concept\": \"BF token dialects with UNKNOWN or UNSEPARATED tokens: new word triads paired like Ook (Meep. Meep? Meep!), emoji BF, CamelCase/no-space words, multi-char glyph units\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detai\n365:  {\"id\": \"netstring-knobs\", \"concept\": \"netstring knobs: len > 1 and mixed lengths, len in UTF-8 bytes vs characters, leading zeros, whitespace/newlines between frames, missing final comma, nested netstrings, frames whose payload is a seen codec\", \"priorit\nTT/Mastery first try (Mastery solve 34.9 s: the solver's own DAYS[27] encoder again was not GM-faithful).\nD28 (\"Our sixteen-fingered friend is walking backwards.\" / \"Back in Sixteen\") left the esolangs after two days and\nREMIXED two early days: D3 HEX (the prompt re-uses D3's \"sixteen-fingered friend\" riddle) + D12 REVERSAL (\"walking\nbackwards\"; title = Back in Black) -> the hex string reversed CHARACTER-wise (220 B, `[0-9a-e]`, ends `...6e4`); Mastery\nline 28 = each 4-5 char tail's hex reversed on its own (8/10 chars). Row 104 (prebuilt tgt:free-over-strict) and\n`decode_chunk` (rev + hex) covered it: race probe CORRECT at start+8 s; TT/Mastery (138 x 28, so