": each number = an old day's codec, \"X invited Y over\" = Y on top) | ROT13 OVER BASE64 (D29):\"\"\")\nold_i = t.index(\"**Days 28-29 (REMIXES of two early codecs).**\")\nold_j = t.index(\"**Day 30: Percent Percent**\")\nt = t[:old_i] + \"\"\"**Day 28: Back in Sixteen** (\"Our sixteen-fingered friend is walking backwards.\"): 220 B `[0-9a-e]` = D3 hex reversed\nCHARACTER-wise (`...6e4`); `bytes.fromhex(t[::-1])` (forward and byte-reversed reads are junk). Race probe CORRECT at\nstart+8 s; TT/Mastery first try; no DAYS[28] registered -- passed only because line 28 was LAST.\n\n**Day 29: Rotten Base** (\"Sixty-four invited thirteen over. Things got scrambled.\" -- ROT13 OVER BASE64).\n- 148-byte `blob.txt`, one line, no newline, `[A-Za-z0-9+/]` ending `ZD==`, len%4==0: std padded base64 of the\n  sentence, then ROT13 over its LETTERS only (digits and `+/=` untouched): `GzywMFO3` = rot13 of `TmljZSB3` \"Nice w\".\n  Pun: the numbers ARE the old days (D1 \"64\", D2's rot13 = 13), \"invited ... over\" = 13 laid on top of 64, \"Rotten\" =\n  ROT + base. Triage's idea list already said \"base64 (64)\" + \"ROT13\".\n- Plain `b64decode` SUCCEEDS into junk (rot13 keeps the charset) -- the cue to undo a free layer first. Command:\n  `python3 -I -c \"import sys,codecs,base64;print(base64.b64decode(codecs.decode(open(sys.argv[1]).read().strip(),'rot13')).decode())\" blob.txt`.\n  GM accepted the slug as printed (pattern + `trim`; no convention change).\n- Single CORRECT at start+35 s, first submit. TT (148 B, same shape) 2.4 s. Mastery 143 x 29 (line 29 = 8-char\n  `xxxxxx==`, e.g. `pP0kAN==` -> `p-14`): first submit 143/143, 4.9 s, because the single worker appended DAYS[29] at\n  runtime (`if _wc.day_codec(29) is None: _wc.DAYS.append((29,\"rot13-b64\",enc,dec,False))`, with DAYS[26]/[27]).\n- \"Had trouble\" in the digest = harness, not solver: all 10 post-run generalize launches and 3 ratchet launches died\n  instantly on the account's weekly rate limit (`out_of_credits`); nothing was re-checked, no answer was wrong. The\n  carried `solver/NOTES.md` still described D25 (copied forward) -- write today's notes over it, don't append.\n- Lesson: second remix day; a prompt that names old day NUMBERS names the layers. Encoder for the lib entry:\n  `codecs.encode(base64.b64encode(s.encode()).decode(),'rot13')`.\n\n\"\"\" + t[old_j:]\nopen(F, 'w').write(t)\nPYEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/tech_edit.py && wc -l reference/techniques/warmups.md && git diff --stat reference/"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1114,"cache_read_input_tokens":95943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1114},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"970ca733-aece-4114-b789-a48808ed5691","uuid":"3b24d8a5-5307-46eb-8e0c-392559857e8d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T04:40:07.244Z","request_id":"req_011CgZhURNacfB36TmbYAGwU","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WGq2ssCdf1zGLxbh8Mm7KJ":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/tech_edit.py <<'PYEOF'\nF = 'reference/techniques/warmups.md'\nt = open(F).read()\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(old) == 1, old[:70]\n    t = t.replace(old, new)\nrep(\"\"\"`codecs.encode(b64encode(s.encode()).decode(),'rot13')` (DAYS[29]: NOT in lib yet).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"`codecs.encode(b64encode(s.encode()).decode(),'rot13')` (lib DAYS[29] `rot13-b64`, byte-exact on 148/148 D30 Mastery\n  line 29). Mastery line 29 values: always a 4-char tail -> 8 chars ending `==` (`pP0kAN==` -> `p-14`), so it is shaped\n  exactly like a line-1 base64 fragment: only the line NUMBER separates them.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"D28 and D29 had\n  no registered codec and passed only because their line was LAST; D30\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"D28 ha